## A6: troubleshooting inventory
117-| `packages/mpd-bundle-plugin/client.js` no longer parses after the browser factories were edited (`SyntaxError: Unexpected token ':'` from every suite that loads the artifact) | the build script splices `src/{web-client,team-page,settings-card}.ts` into the artifact **as TEXT**, so raw TypeScript reached a browser bundle. The build now erases types itself before splicing (`stripTypeScriptTypes(…, { mode: "strip" })` — the same transform the runtime applies, which keeps comments and the factory line boundaries the boundary searches rely on). Rebuild with `node scripts/build-mpd-client.ts`, confirm `node --check packages/mpd-bundle-plugin/client.js`, and never hand-edit the artifact. |
118-| a tool that reads a `packages/*/src/*.ts` file as TEXT breaks after that file became TypeScript | any text consumer of a TypeScript source (the client splice above, a fixture that `eval`s source, a needle that greps for an exact declaration) must run the text through Node's own `stripTypeScriptTypes(…, { mode: "strip" })` first, or match on SHAPE rather than on one spelling of a declaration. Measured twice in this wave: the client splice and `packages/mpd-bundle-plugin/test/*` reading `src/*.js` by literal path; a third instance was a QA needle pinned to a local variable's name (`parsed` → `fields`), repaired by matching the claim instead of the identifier. |
119:| a reader asks why the tree still carries `.js` files after the JavaScript→TypeScript wave | exactly **57** remain (measured 2026-10-21), and the reason is MEASURED rather than habitual: Node refuses type stripping for any file whose resolved path is under `node_modules` (`ERR_UNSUPPORTED_NODE_MODULES_TYPE_STRIPPING` — measured BOTH for an import and for a direct `node <path>.ts` invocation), and a shipped bundle IS installed at `<profile>/node_modules/@mpd-dsh/mpd`. The 57 are: 33 `packages/*/dist/**` build artifacts (the loader imports them as `.../dist/index.js`, and `bun build` emits JavaScript by definition); 2 browser bundles — `packages/mpd-bundle-plugin/client.js` and the adopted `packages/mpd-bundle-plugin/adopted/agent-teams-client.js` (upstream bytes spliced VERBATIM); and 22 upstream skill-corpus files — 19 under `skills/ulw-research/scripts/*.mjs`, `skills/visual-qa/scripts/visual-qa.mjs` (generated from `skills/visual-qa/scripts/cli.ts` and run with `node`), and 2 `skills/ultimate-browsing/engine/templates/*.js` (Playwright templates the vendored engine drives with `node`). Everything else this repository owns is `.ts`, and a genuine CommonJS module is `.cts` — **convert one and it works from a checkout while the SAME file throws the error above from an installed bundle.** The converted ADOPTED body carries `@ts-nocheck` and its suite is `tsconfig.json`-excluded ON PURPOSE: it is vendored code renamed for the source-language rule, never code this repository types — typing it is a deliberate project, not a cleanup. Evidence: `evidence/ts-cordis-conformance/`. |
120-| an evidence write lands somewhere nobody aimed at — `bash: line 1: /logs/baseline-bun-test-bundle-plugin.log: No such file or directory`, or worse, a file appears in an unrelated tree and nothing reported an error | a shell variable built from a **command substitution whose failure was not checked**, used as a **REDIRECT TARGET**. Measured 2026-10-06 (wave `dag-edges-scroll`, the verifier's own first attempt): `TS=$(cat /tmp/verify_ts.txt) && OUT="evidence/<wave>/verify/$TS" && mkdir -p "$OUT/logs" && { …; } > "$OUT/logs/x.log" 2>&1`. The bash tool gives **every call a FRESH `/tmp`** (T-23 above), so `/tmp/verify_ts.txt` did not exist, `cat` failed, `TS` came back EMPTY, and `$OUT/logs/x.log` degraded to the ROOT-ANCHORED absolute path `/logs/x.log`. That run failed harmlessly ONLY because `/logs` did not exist — **the dangerous half is that if the parent directory HAPPENS to exist, the write lands there SILENTLY and no gate sees it.** Any wave script building an evidence path from `$(cat f)`, `$(mktemp)`, `$(date …)` or an unvalidated `$1` is one existing directory away from writing into an unrelated tree. **Fix, and it is a standing rule: every redirect target in an evidence/QA script is a LITERAL path, never one assembled through an unvalidated variable; if a variable must be used, assert non-empty AND that the resolved parent exists BEFORE the redirect (`[ -n "$TS" ] || exit 1`); prefer a `node`/`bun` file write, which throws on a bad path, over shell redirection, which mostly does not.** An UNRESOLVED instance of this class is recorded rather than explained: roughly 300 lines of unrelated output (a `no-terminal-writes --self-test` transcript and a root `bun test` run) were spliced into the middle of a reviewer's `findings.md` between that seat's own writes, and no command of any seat named that path — **attribution stays open**, and the mechanism is NOT this one, because the measured redirect ENOENT'd before writing a byte. |
